# playpick cell: mode=daily boss=cold spec=warrior:protection style=idle
# view=1280x800 save=fresh. boss=cold is playpick's own filler label -- daily's
# boss axis is not reachable as a playpick axis (direction.md's standing note,
# reconfirmed by this session's own probe: 2026-10-02-19-probe.play). Today's
# actual daily, read off the probe's daily-screen.png, is The Bonegrinder,
# 25-player, normal, SWARMING (twice as many thralls, half as often).
#
# What is new here: sessions.jsonl has no prior mode=daily + style=idle +
# warrior:protection reading in any combination (ten prior warrior:protection
# sessions span good/melee/mash/idle, but the one idle reading is mode=raid,
# 10-normal, not a daily and not this affix), and no prior idle-style tank
# reading against The Bonegrinder at 25-player at all -- every idle tank
# reading on record is either 10-player or against a different boss. SWARMING
# doubles the thrall count the tank would otherwise be picking up, so this
# tests whether an idle tank still costs the raid nothing once the one
# mechanic a tank actually answers (thralls) is turned up.
#
# class:0 is Warrior Tank -- the daily screen's own grid only exposes numeric
# class:N labels, not the class:spec:role labels the composition screen uses
# (read off the probe's daily-screen.png: row 1 is Warrior Tank, Warrior DPS,
# Paladin Tank, Paladin Heal, Paladin DPS).
open
tap daily
targets
shot daily-screen
tap class:0
shot class-selected
tap start
waitscreen fight 15
state
targets
ui
play idle 80
bill
state
shot mid1
play idle 80
bill
state
shot mid2
play idle 80
bill
state
says
shot end
